  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nRain chances will continue from the Coastal Plains to the Victoria \nCrossroads ahead of the approaching front. While we are still in a \nMarginal Risk for severe thunderstorms and excessive rainfall, \nconfidence on that occurring is dropping by the hour. Hazards from \nthis system will begin tonight with Gale force winds over the gulf \nwaters and a high risk of rip currents and coastal flooding along \nthe coast. This front will usher below normal temperatures with \nhighs Monday and Tuesday in the 60s and lows in the 40s and 50s.\n\nMinor coastal flooding is expected to continue tonight into early \nMonday morning as strong northeasterly winds enhance the Ekman \ntransport mechanism along with sufficient wave run-up from 8-9 \nsecond swell periods. There is a high risk of rip currents tonight \nthrough Monday, leading to especially dangerous swimming conditions. \nMinor coastal flooding may continue to be a concern into the middle \nof next week during high tide at night.",
